(footprint "noknok_FlashPads_USB-module_1x4_M2.5"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "noknok flashing interface for CH32V203 USB modules. Mounting hole at ORIGIN (0,0): M2.5, 2.5mm NPTH (Adafruit/Qwiic-aligned, nylon screw+standoff kit e.g. Adafruit 3299). 4 single-side SMD pogo pads (1=GND, 2=SWDIO, 3=VCC, 4=SWCLK) round Ø1.5mm on 2.54mm pitch, copper+mask only (NO paste); pad row offset +X and 1.25mm up (Y=-1.25), GND-to-hole = 3.75mm (~0.6mm pad-to-standoff clearance = metal-safe). No RESET pad - WCH-LinkE connects via SWDIO+SWCLK alone (2-wire SWD), same reasoning as the CH32V003 single-wire variant needing no RST. SINGLE merged courtyard (hole keepout + pad strip as one F.CrtYd outline). The embedded hole sets the hole-to-pad spacing AND is the pogo-clamp orientation key. Authored on F.Cu - FLIP to bottom for bottom-side flashing. Shared-jig geometry with noknok_FlashPads_I2C-module: SWCLK sits at +2.54mm past VCC (same GND/SWIO(SWDIO)/VCC offsets as the I2C 3-pad part), so ONE 4-pogo jig services both I2C modules (3 pogos used) and USB modules (all 4). Standard placement: hole at 2.25mm/2.25mm from the board corner, matching the I2C modules.")
	(tags "noknok flash pogo SWDIO SWCLK CH32V203 USB programming testpad M2.5")
	(attr exclude_from_pos_files exclude_from_bom)
